# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing here belongs in version control.
#
# The secrets section is the one that matters. A committed .env puts the JWT
# signing keys and the encryption key into the history permanently — rewriting
# history does not help once a repository has been cloned or pushed, and those
# keys are enough to mint a session for any account and read every TOTP seed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Anything that looks like key material, wherever it lands.
*.pem
*.key
# A personal access token was being kept here. The name is not covered by any
# rule above, so `git add .` would have committed it.
gittoken.md
*.p12
*.keystore
secrets/

# ── member data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KYC documents and ticket attachments. Identity documents in a git history are
# a breach that cannot be undone.
storage/
backend/storage/
ops/backups/
*.sql
*.sql.gz
!backend/prisma/migrations/**/*.sql

# ── dependencies and build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── test and tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# ── logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── editors and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── local scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.cache/
tmp/

# Competitor research captures.
# Excluded deliberately: research/ holds scraped pages and logged-in
# screenshots from a third-party platform, including real members' names and
# account IDs. That is other people's personal data and must not be published.
# Remove this rule only if the captures have been scrubbed.
research/

# Local mirror of fyntrust.io, kept as a porting reference. 83 MB, three
# quarters of which is one PDF — it is a working copy of a site we already
# own, not source, so it stays out of the history. Re-create it with
# Doc/reference/fyntrust/mirror.py if it is needed again.
Doc/reference/fyntrust/

# Published app builds. The APK is a build artefact served off the server, not
# source — and at several megabytes it has no business in the history.
ops/downloads/

# ── source asset drops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Originals handed over for the redesign. The versions the app actually serves
# live under frontend/public/, so committing these too would duplicate ~7MB of
# binaries in the history for no benefit. They stay on disk, untracked.
/HeroSectionvideo.mp4
/home_new_rwo5_img_01.png
/deposit-bonus-banner-img-20240110.png
/category-market-analysis-banner-img.png
